a self-described \"rough patch\" over the past two seasons, Clemson coach Dabo Swinney is resolute in his belief that he and the Tigers have a lot more wins ahead of them.","published":"2026-11-17T20:37:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512833/defiant-dabo-swinney-says-clemson-gonna-win-bunch-more","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Army OC Cody Worley to be Furman head coach","description":"Army offensive coordinator Cody Worley is expected to be the next head coach at Furman, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-17T20:11:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512672/army-oc-worley-furman-head-coach","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Former Iowa State AD calls NIL system 'money laundering'","description":"Former Iowa State athletic director Jamie Pollard delivered a scorching appraisal of college athletics to the Knight Commission, equating NIL as a money-laundering operation.","published":"2026-11-17T19:08:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50512485/former-iowa-state-ad-calls-nil-system-money-laundering","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Purdue rolls with FAA ground stop by taking buses to Iowa","description":"Unable to travel by plane, the Boilermakers rolled with the situation and found some good times on the way.","published":"2026-11-17T11:28:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504665/purdue-faa-ground-stop-bus-iowa","type":"Story","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Heisman of Week 11: Duke's Nate Sheppard has entered the running","description":"In a season in which star running backs seem to be popping up out of nowhere, the Blue Devils' sophomore stands out.","published":"2026-11-17T14:55:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503621/heisman-watch-week-11-duke-nate-sheppard","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on College Football Playoff bubble ahead of committee's third ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-17T22:28:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503628/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-third-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5154734/griffin-wilde","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Griffin_Wilde"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Griffin Wilde","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Griffin_Wilde","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:24Z","intro":"Griffin Wilde is an American college football wide receiver for the Northwestern Wildcats. He previously played for the South Dakota State Jackrabbits.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Wilde attended Thomas Jefferson High School in Sioux Falls, South Dakota. Over his junior and senior seasons he combined for 100 receptions for 1,858 yards with 22 touchdowns. Wilde committed to South Dakota State University to play college football. He also played basketball in high school."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Wilde was a starter his true freshman year at South Dakota State in 2023 and had 20 receptions for 399 yards and six touchdowns. He became the Jackrabbits number one receiver in 2024, recording 71 receptions for 1,147 yards and 12 touchdowns. After the season, Wilde entered the transfer portal and transferred to Northwestern University. He was a starter his first year at Northwestern in 2025. In their upset victory over the Penn State Nittany Lions, he had seven receptions for 94 yards and a touchdown. Wilde was named MVP of the 2025 GameAbove Sports Bowl. In 2026, Wilde faced his former team and recorded three receptions for 104 yards in an 34-18 win."}]}}